  "scope": "Native GR0/C797 context discovery, private aligned/cleared storage, golden/regular promotion, private barrier through actual Device/Runtime/GPFIFO. Rendering, public render queue and descriptors remain open.",
  "contract": "No public ABI, kernel or library change. Existing BO descriptor/alignment and RM ownership.",
  "validation": {
    "final_attribution": "Unit run precedes attribution-only comment/license and module-version updates; final driver build includes them.",
    "device_model": "Six bounded scenarios: complete golden/regular + two barriers; missing class; GR allocation rejection; semaphore timeout; promotion rejection; changed promotion reply.",
    "guest": "No new run: QEMU cannot execute this NVIDIA GR path; unchanged public ABI.",
    "nvidia_cases": 51,
    "build_steps": 7,
    "inventoried_checks": 743,
    "original_c": "NVIDIA570.144: GR allocation16, barrier44, static query1664, golden/regular promotion560 each, flags32.",
    "new_recurring_gates": 0
  },
  "decisions": [
    "RM kernel client already uses processID=ffffffff and empty name, matching Nouveau; private allocation requests kernel-privileged memory.",
    "GPU-cached backing follows kernel_graphics_context.c; physical initialization attributes use its separate GPU_CACHEABLE_NO value4.",
    "Golden scheduling admitted after promotion and before GR allocation; no host methods on privileged channel; disable/free ACK before regular context.",
    "Global buffers held by context-child dependency until regular group retires; no duplicate initialization or unbounded lifetime table.",
    "4K RM page mappings retained; larger physical/VA alignment is accounted at the canonical BO granule."
  ],
